\name{semantica_execute}\alias{semantica_execute}\title{Execute an inspected SEMANTICA run plan}\usage{semantica_execute(plan, llm = NULL, ...)}\arguments{\item{plan}{A \code{semantica_run_plan}.}\item{llm}{Optional backend/configuration override, including credentials or custom backend components that are deliberately not stored in plans.}\item{...}{Named overrides passed to \code{semantica_run()}.}}\description{Delegates directly to \code{semantica_run()} using the specification stored by \code{semantica_run_plan()}.}\value{A compact \code{semantica_run_result}; its \code{advanced} field retains the complete canonical \code{semantica_full_pipeline_result}.}
